1
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
You can't escape history.

2
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Donner Pass is a horror film directed by Elise Robertson.

3
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Donner Pass has a well-known and macabre history - the place where George Donner and his party got stuck
in the winter of 1846 and were forced to resort to cannibalism to keep from starving.

4
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
But what if it wasn't just history?

5
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
Kayley, played by Desiree Hall.

6
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Thomas, played by Erik Stocklin.

7
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Nicole, played by Adelaide Kane.

8
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Valerie, played by Krystal Davis.

9
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Donner Pass is a 7,056-foot-high (2,151 m) mountain pass in the northern Sierra Nevada, above Donner
Lake and Donner Memorial State Park about 9 miles (14 km) west of Truckee, California.

10
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Like the Sierra Nevada itself, the pass has a steep approach from
the east and a gradual approach from the west.

11
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
The pass has been used by the California Trail, First transcontinental railroad,
Overland Route, Lincoln Highway and Victory Highway (both later U.S.

12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Route 40 and still later Donner Pass Road), as
well as indirectly by Interstate 80.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
The pass gets its name from the ill-fated Donner
Party who overwintered there in 1846.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Today, the area is home to a thriving recreational community with several alpine
lakes and ski resorts (Donner Ski Ranch, Boreal, and Sugar Bowl).

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
The permanent communities in the area include Kingvale and Soda Springs, as well
as the larger community below the pass surrounding Donner Lake.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
The film explores themes of curse, cannibal, vanity project, woman director.

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
The tone is dark.
